   "label": "Co-branding isn’t a trend. It’s a power move.�Local brands are teaming up to win market share, relevance, and attention faster than ever. When both names bring real value, co-branding becomes a shortcut to visibility, trial, and cultural buzz.\n\nHere’s how brands in Egypt are doing it right 👇\n\n1. Kraft Heinz  × Chipsy (PepsiCo Egypt) �A flavor-packed drop. Chipsy launched limited sandwich-inspired chips using Heinz’s iconic sauces. Ketchup, BBQ, and Burger all made the cut.\n\n1. V7 × DARA’s Ice Cream�Summer in a cup. A zesty pink lemonade born from V7’s soda and DARA’s playful twist.\n\n2. Dolato Gelateria  × Juhayna�Artisan gelato powered by rich Egyptian dairy. Dolato used Juhayna’s milk to bring creamy authenticity to every scoop.\n\n3. Lychee Egypt x DARA’s Ice Cream�Texture meets taste. DARA’s honeycomb chunks folded into Lychee’s smooth vanilla yogurt.\n\n4. Schweppes × Everyday Roastery Coffee �Fizz with flair. Schweppes created in-store specialty drinks with Everyday Roastery using its bold soda lineup.\n\n5. Juhayna x Copa Acai �Clean fuel. Smoothies and Greek yogurt co-created to deliver both flavor and function.\n\nBut here’s the catch ⚠️�You can’t borrow credibility if you haven’t built it.\nThe Board Consulting\nVideo length:0minutes; 7seconds\nAug 8, 2025 \n 71 views",
